 ],
 "literal": "White glory lily's opening buds, fresh-flowered jasmine, / with fragrant-petaled blue water lily, interspersed and mixed, / like a garland of excellent delicate stringing, / the fragrant good woman's body / is softer than a tender shoot, and is sweet indeed to embrace.",
 "translation": "Like a beautifully strung garland, where the opening buds of the white glory lily and fresh jasmines are interspersed and woven together with fragrant-petaled blue water lilies, the fragrant body of my good woman is softer than a tender sprout, and is so sweet to embrace.",
 "modern": "வெண்காந்தளின் விரியும் மொட்டுகளும், புதிய முல்லைப் பூக்களும், நறுமணமுள்ள இதழ்களைக் கொண்ட குவளைப் பூக்களோடு இடையிடையே கலந்து, நுட்பமாகத் தொடுக்கப்பட்ட மாண்புடைய மாலை போல, நறிய நல்லவளின் மேனி தளிர் இலையை விட மென்மையானது; தழுவுவதற்கும் மிகவும் இனியது.",
 "explanation": "The hero speaks to himself in delight after embracing his beloved, praising her exquisite beauty and softness. He compares her fragrant body to a finely crafted garland woven with opening buds of white glory lily, fresh jasmine, and fragrant blue water lilies. These flowers belong to the Kuriñci landscape, symbolizing the lushness and natural beauty of their mountain home. He declares that her skin is even softer than a tender green shoot and is incredibly sweet to embrace. The key words are 'கோதை போல' (like a garland) and 'முயங்கற்கும் இனிதே' (sweet to embrace).",
